 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "The angels are never drawn or symbolised; Ibrahim and his wife get no plate, figure or drop. A scroll for «بالبشرى» (the news as a message, after Ibrahim's name; a gold burst could read as the angels), a house for his hospitality («فما لبث أن جاء بعجل حنيذ»); no calf, hands or people drawn. 71:1-2 «قائمة» is not glossed: the tafsirs differ (serving the guests / listening behind the curtain). No plate on «إسحاق» or «يعقوب». The plan's title «ضيف إبراهيم» is Quran wording (15:51, 51:24): now «بشارة الملائكة». STAGING v4: Restaged under Staging v4, as in 15_51-60: Ibrahim is a blue drop labelled Ibrahim, his guests one gold angel drop labelled the angels (neither tafsir gives their number), in his home by day (As-Sa'di: he hurried to his house). c1 (69-70): the angels appear on 69:2 and glow softly on 69:3; a scroll plate for the good news (69:5-7, after Ibrahim's name); the greeting is spoken by the angels (69:6) and returned by Ibrahim (69:8), each toward the other drop; on 69:13 Ibrahim's drop moves toward his guests (As-Sa'di: he brought it near them); no food, calf or plate is drawn. 70: no gesture for his unease (Al-Muyassar: he concealed it), the camera holds wide; the angels speak (70:11). No plate for the angels or their mission, no close-up and no pan on the drops. c2 (71-72): Sarah is never drawn, and nothing acts her standing, her laughter or her words (72 is held wide with no speech beat). The good news (71:4, Al-Muyassar: on the tongues of the angels) is marked only by a soft glow of the angels' drop, with no speech arc (an arc would aim at Ibrahim, while the news is addressed to his wife); a seal plate for the good news (71:4-9, a safe plate over the names of Ishaq and Ya'qub), an hourglass for old age (72:5-8). No light or plate on the name of the son. Cover: the angels greeting Ibrahim in his home, scroll plate on."
 },
